{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":370429,"duration_api_ms":256938,"ttft_ms":2558,"num_turns":30,"result":"## Summary\n\n**EXP-003: RAG few-shot** — **quality 0.320** (dev), new best (+0.013 vs baseline 0.307)\n\n**What I did:** Created `GoldExemplars.swift` with 12 hard-coded non-dev gold examples. At runtime, for each input, retrieve the 2 nearest exemplars by Jaccard word-overlap similarity and inject them as concrete few-shot demonstrations in the system prompt. Single FM call.\n\n**Result:** \n- 0.320 vs previous best 0.307 — modest but real improvement\n- First tie vs gold (learn_guitar — model asked about guitar type which gold missed)\n- Non-redundancy improved 3→4 across dev cases\n\n**Judge notes insight:** The RAG examples taught the model better redundancy avoidance, but catastrophic coverage failures persist — the model still asks \"What is the name of your bakery?\" for a naming task, and misses critical unknowns (budget for dinner party, departure city for Paris trip). The 3B model sees the good examples but still can't reliably transfer the \"which unknown is most decision-critical\" reasoning to novel task types. Next hypothesis should target this specific failure mode more aggressively (e.g., a chain-of-thought reasoning step asking \"what single fact would most change the plan?\" before generating questions).","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0d29d5b9-1e74-49f2-be70-e41a5215bbde","total_cost_usd":0.47748925000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34611,"cache_read_input_tokens":438120,"output_tokens":14375,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":34611},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":311,"cache_read_input_tokens":33611,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_to